<%# locals: (sections:) %>
<%# The outline of a long page (Belegungstabelle F46): the sections of THIS page as a
    list of links, with a mark on the one the reader is in. For a page that is one
    long column of sections (the preferences), so a reader in the middle of it can
    see where they are and go elsewhere without scrolling back up.

    sections: [{ label:, anchor: }] in page order; anchor is the id of the section.

    The links are plain #anchors: they jump, change the address and work with Back
    without any script. page_outline_controller only adds the mark
    (aria-current="location"); its look is components/page_outline.css.

    One list, two layouts (rule 7: moved, never shrunk):
    - from lg on a column of its own beside the content, which the caller makes
      stick (the API tokens' explainer stands the same way): quiet words on a thin
      line, the current one in ink with a 2px stroke on the edge that faces the
      content (F6 in its form without a fill, as a tab's);
    - below lg one row under the page head that scrolls sideways without a
      scrollbar (as the tab row does), the words underlined: they act on this page
      and lead nowhere else (F4).

    ⚠️ It is no tab row. A tab is a page of its own with an address of its own; these
    are places on one page. That is why the row has no stroke under the current
    word and the words are underlined, which tabs never are.

    ⚠️ Not for a page with a lane: a #anchor there reads as a lane change
    (app/javascript/controllers/CLAUDE.md). No margin or padding to the page edge:
    the edge belongs to the layout (spec/views/one_page_edge_guard_spec.rb). %>
<% label = t('navigation.on_this_page') %>
<nav class="page-outline" aria-label="<%= label %>" data-controller="page-outline">
  <%# The name of the list for the eye; the nav's aria-label says it to a screen reader. %>
  <p class="mb-2 hidden ps-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted lg:block" aria-hidden="true"><%= label %></p>
  <ul class="scrollbar-hide flex gap-x-5 overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap text-sm lg:block lg:overflow-visible lg:whitespace-normal lg:border-s lg:border-divider">
    <% sections.each do |section| %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to section.fetch(:label), "##{section.fetch(:anchor)}",
              class: 'page-outline__link inline-block py-1 font-medium text-body underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-heading ' \
                     'lg:-ms-px lg:block lg:border-s-2 lg:border-transparent lg:ps-3 lg:font-normal lg:text-muted lg:no-underline',
              data: { page_outline_target: 'link', action: 'page-outline#jump' } %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</nav>
